= Ambiguity — Simple =

'''Ambiguity''' means that a word, phrase, or sentence can be understood in more than one way.

The word “bank” can mean a financial institution or the side of a river.

A whole sentence can also be ambiguous because of its structure. “I saw the person with the telescope” can mean that I used a telescope, or that the person had one.

[[Context (linguistics)/Simple|Context]] often helps people choose the intended meaning.

Ambiguity is not exactly the same as vagueness. Vagueness usually means that a word has blurry boundaries. Ambiguity means there are distinguishable interpretations.

[[Polysemy/Simple|Polysemy]] is one kind of lexical phenomenon where one word has several related senses.

